B.a9J=new A.cn("n01","A Tafel slope of 42 mV/dec | indicated a rate-determining | first electron transfer.")
B.a9G=new A.cn("n02","The (111) reflection at 2\u03b8 = 43.6\xb0 | broadened as | the crystallite size fell.")
B.a9C=new A.cn("n03","Scherrer analysis gave | a crystallite size of 8.4 \xb1 0.6 nm | for the calcined powder.")
B.aa0=new A.cn("n04","Extended X-ray absorption fine structure | resolved a Ni\u2013O coordination number | of 4.2.")
B.aa5=new A.cn("n05","A gas hourly space velocity of 24,000 mL/g/h | was held | for the entire run.")
B.aa1=new A.cn("n06","Sulfur was kept below 50 ppm | to avoid | irreversible poisoning.")
B.a9T=new A.cn("n07","Ostwald ripening coarsened the particles, | whereas encapsulation | suppressed coalescence.")
B.a9M=new A.cn("n08","The kinetics followed | a Mars\u2013van Krevelen mechanism | rather than Langmuir\u2013Hinshelwood.")
B.a9S=new A.cn("n09","The area-specific resistance rose | to 0.31 \u03a9 cm\xb2 | after five hundred hours.")
B.a9y=new A.cn("n10","Diffraction used Cu K\u03b1 radiation | with \u03bb = 1.5406 \xc5 | at room temperature.")
B.a9Q=new A.cn("n11","The adsorption enthalpy \u0394H | was \u221278 kJ/mol | on the stepped facet.")
B.a9D=new A.cn("n12","Electrical conductivity reached | 3.6 \xd7 10\u207b\xb2 S/cm | after carbonisation.")
